ne our systems.\n\n- System I is decoupled since its equations depend on only one variable each. Indeed, ${x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-12{x}_{1}(t)$ depends on only ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}^{′}(t)=5{x}_{2}(t)$ depends on only ${x}_{2}(t).$\n\n- System II is *not* decoupled because some of its equations depend on more than one variable. For example, ${x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)$ depends on ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$\n\n- System III is *not* decoupled because some of its equations depend on more than one variable. For example, ${x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+6{x}_{2}(t)$ depends on ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-331976/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "276898e7-57a4-5ca6-8df7-99fd318a2702"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-331976"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-331114/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "a56bb6a6-7298-5f6c-b07b-8d4f41a2fdd1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331114/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "94de02c7-3039-539e-a104-81cb024a30ff" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331114/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "7e3d6d8c-858e-5ae2-8438-6020e1961207" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331114/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "7456163a-d835-5f26-a20b-4606dd716f99" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331114/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "8472f07b-9650-5a8c-a1ce-334cac40df93" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331114/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa51fdba-a662-51c7-92b8-80485563989a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-331114/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-331114/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-331114/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-331114/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" "q-331114/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-331114/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331114" :question/id #uuid "d2403e2c-333c-55ea-8911-693b14f580bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-331114" :question/problem "Which of the following systems of linear ODEs are decoupled?\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=6{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=5{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-8{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$" :question/worked-solution "A *decoupled system* consists of equations depending on only one variable, such as\n\n$$\n{x}_{i}^{′}(t)={\\lambda }_{i}{x}_{i}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\lambda }_{i}$ is a constant. This means that we can solve each equation independently. \n\nWith this in mind, let's examine our systems.\n\n- System I is *not* decoupled because some of its equations depend on more than one variable. For example, ${x}_{1}^{′}(t)=6{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t)$ depends on ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$\n\n- System II is decoupled since its equations depend on only one variable each. Indeed, ${x}_{1}^{′}(t)=5{x}_{1}(t)$ depends on only ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-8{x}_{2}(t)$ depends on only ${x}_{2}(t).$\n\n- System III is *not* decoupled because some of its equations depend on more than one variable. For example, ${x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)$ depends on ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-331114/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "276898e7-57a4-5ca6-8df7-99fd318a2702"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-331114"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-321897"] :question/problem "Which of the following systems of linear ODEs are decoupled?\n\n- ${x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]x(t)$\n- ${x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)$\n- ${x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]x(t)$" :question/worked-solution "A *decoupled system* consists of equations depending on only one variable, such as\n\n$$\n{x}_{i}^{′}(t)={\\lambda }_{i}{x}_{i}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\lambda }_{i}$ is a constant. This means that we can solve each equation independently. \n\nIn matrix form, a linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ is decoupled if $A$ is a diagonal matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's examine our systems.\n\n- Systems I and III are decoupled since their corresponding matrices are diagonal.\n\n- System II is *not* decoupled because its matrix is not diagonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-332537/selection/1d70c3cb036be66c8d3a7581c62d96ce3a2b00a13d1efa01a309bb61d31cdb29" :answer/id #uuid "c5bafbc8-b733-5d8a-bcf6-d414ce6245d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-5t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332537/selection/30866f21518734b6ae0839e135cba768b2829a6b2dc96203c52b1ede96b919d2" :answer/id #uuid "7b4ebf76-2ed3-5b1e-932a-7bf5e43605c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1}\\in R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332537/selection/7164f103184953042ccc8d64101acd13f0bb6492e5365d1215bd3bf630ee62e8" :answer/id #uuid "e44b2e20-2d14-5704-9f76-1d143dc97fdb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-5t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332537/selection/341c6664e737b60ddfcf2cbf543592f28b0298b2b0e871ceb56b4964d30f03f6" :answer/id #uuid "655af992-dd3c-5469-8025-461cc357d5eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-10t},\\,{c}_{1}\\in R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332537/selection/ae2571a0a268e4f58004bee6ed76118ab22b738dc016b4906798181af1a294b1" :answer/id #uuid "bc6d2fbd-15b8-504d-a62f-2c5693f9c95f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332537/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f2bfbe53-328d-565d-a2d8-e6b00356014e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-332537/selection/7164f103184953042ccc8d64101acd13f0bb6492e5365d1215bd3bf630ee62e8" :answer-field/choices ["q-332537/selection/1d70c3cb036be66c8d3a7581c62d96ce3a2b00a13d1efa01a309bb61d31cdb29" "q-332537/selection/30866f21518734b6ae0839e135cba768b2829a6b2dc96203c52b1ede96b919d2" "q-332537/selection/7164f103184953042ccc8d64101acd13f0bb6492e5365d1215bd3bf630ee62e8" "q-332537/selec