45cd5ea9b7178f7f9940fc612a65dfd472f63804385f66ab621a5eda3f" "q-79669/selection/577d188d2ca525810782a250088aabdf55be4f115d00ef7552ee40f67f1fcf39" "q-79669/selection/1630e49c59fb0ba18a38e3ec6b06ee0fba23b1ba813a3d30e46fe8999778ec02"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79669" :question/id #uuid "5586f2bf-d487-5c34-8679-0141d368b6a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-79669" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the system of differential equations\n${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=7{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}$" :question/worked-solution "Given a decoupled system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {\\lambda }_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write our differential equation in matrix form:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSince the matrix of the differential system is diagonal, the system is decoupled. \n\nTherefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{7t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79669/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce35e5a9-2444-5e5f-9463-5a4d54496d9d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79669"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-39731/selection/33eb72f2f295f79fb6da55322fe45c5e5aeb715f1132b0d347782e4b78340fc9" :answer/id #uuid "4c02e2ac-4421-5b53-82c0-ad171c07d270" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ e\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{2}^{-2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39731/selection/21d3bc8eb2536dff5007d0867e3621c391efee142a836f94e3f03681c2393136" :answer/id #uuid "17b65272-8fd6-5e56-b64b-a0371b2b2cf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}e \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]{2}^{-2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39731/selection/d483112b324e9d23b046497e433d14d9a9e1dbd66965dcabd128311d2c3df095" :answer/id #uuid "c86f6434-47d6-51e2-a475-9ff5113a912b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}e \\\\ 4e\\end{aligned}]5{e}^{2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39731/selection/7c15dc074711a5c13f7d296c55d3a4014936d6d417e3b2ee456e49f97c615172" :answer/id #uuid "0b199979-074c-5722-ba9c-06f9598c1d2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}e \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39731/selection/1a4afb6a7b984cd2faea1628a91410a96b4587e32231bf324e0000b1d3677168" :answer/id #uuid "4e9bdb75-752e-5d54-8527-62a39c6d8706" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}e \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]{2}^{-2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39731/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "13e41a67-cbd9-53ff-a330-15d9bd48f947" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-39731/selection/21d3bc8eb2536dff5007d0867e3621c391efee142a836f94e3f03681c2393136" :answer-field/choices ["q-39731/selection/33eb72f2f295f79fb6da55322fe45c5e5aeb715f1132b0d347782e4b78340fc9" "q-39731/selection/21d3bc8eb2536dff5007d0867e3621c391efee142a836f94e3f03681c2393136" "q-39731/selection/d483112b324e9d23b046497e433d14d9a9e1dbd66965dcabd128311d2c3df095" "q-39731/selection/7c15dc074711a5c13f7d296c55d3a4014936d6d417e3b2ee456e49f97c615172" "q-39731/selection/1a4afb6a7b984cd2faea1628a91410a96b4587e32231bf324e0000b1d3677168"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-39731" :question/id #uuid "1d9f0640-7a67-5743-954f-f120eaaa869b" :question/math-academy-id "q-39731" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(1)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{6} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We have a decoupled system. Therefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)})}^{-2t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{2}^{-2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(1)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{6} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=1$ into the general solution, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(1) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {2}^{-2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{e}^{6} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}{e}^{5} \\\\ \\frac{{c}_{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}e \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =e[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}+4[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{2}^{-2t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}e \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]{2}^{-2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-39731/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cec0e48f-9fbb-5ada-b7fd-0d389d1b7438"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-39731"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332709/selection/3f7c55c7ef8b8497e29de85a801a186ebb5627c776c49bc00c156a182c426766" :answer/id #uuid "6c7c4b9b-c097-5350-8c33-40ed885488a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332709/selection/390a80a4c6cd0ad76622a7537f99611da9e8c09381696a8ad7c0c1c5e1596937" :answer/id #uuid "e22b9551-1e09-5698-a1cc-2b51e0b62ac4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332709/selection/df14937c0e2275e54cc45e9de08d38086fe22643adc456f74cfa24eb8ca63094" :answer/id #uuid "62c3e270-cb53-555e-a5ee-40a73df6641c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332709/selection/de0ba3f318fa8473b25b75b891d2d259cc924b3c45d82efb149ada1a162a164c" :answer/id #uuid "1c03a1ad-0b0b-58e3-996c-3be326961baf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332709/selection/f4771195542bd12778f8a0f6ec77f47989e5ca894e4b22a4534ae1fa9e8720ff" :answer/id #uuid "b8e72d98-15fa-55f0-9501-32d8088d03e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332709/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b80a2fe0-8080-5d8a-bda5-f8e404f61b63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-332709/selection/df14937c0e2275e54cc45e9de08d38086fe22643adc456f74cfa24eb8ca63094" :answer-field/choices ["q-332709/selection/3f7c55c7ef8b8497e29de85a801a186ebb5627c776c49bc00c156a182c426766" "q-332709/selection/390a80a4c6cd0ad76622a7537f99611da9e8c09381696a8ad7c0c1c5e1596937" "q-332709/selection/df14937c0e2275e54cc45e9de08d38086fe22643adc456f74cfa24eb8ca63094" "q-332709/selection/de0ba3f318fa8473b25b75b891d2d259cc924b3c45d82efb149ada1a162a164c" "q-332709/selection/f4771195542bd12778f8a0f6ec77f47989e5ca894e4b22a4534ae1fa9e8720ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332709" :question/id #uuid "5620c47b-4e97-5ced-9381-5d5cc172acfd" :question/math-academy-id "q-332709" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We have a decoupled system. Therefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =(-3)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}+6\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332709/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cec0e48f-9fbb-5ada-b7fd-0d389d1b7438"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332709"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-168915/selection/308ff9a17aa98dbca82d5392a2b9f27bc530d98cf03a2265d0d33aae3a283544" :answer/id #uuid "b5838c9e-46de-560a-9116-184a1cbb51a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-1} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{-3}\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-168915/selection/f56249ca5a5eb9a722d9560b0d969e55cfbe78fcd91164d91aff407a416e98b0" :answer/id #uuid "75ba1b53-c17b-500e-9d18-8c51503af391" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -{e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-168915/selection/f083c172cff50ef1b5db3ddb2b53cb5cf94037d4eb64381d570a95d999942d12" :answer/id #uuid "d77b23e5-8b44-558f-830b-d98944104c99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -e\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-168915/selection/9117ee8e5cf9bfe4d16f1a3c00f2f3ceaf688cfd6a5494efb43d7b70fb965afa" :answer/id #uuid "f947c65d-7bdd-5e30-ae02-895068997b9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -{e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-168915/selection/2566b7de21c1a242869bd1f8943f91906094c82ae33ab3c11392b9c6a4fee6db" :answer/id #uuid "cdd8f5ae-b802-5f94-a7b7-970e7dcc2383" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -e\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-168915/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "83f95817-0825-505f-9373-1b2c8c3f0f07" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-168915/selection/f56249ca5a5eb9a722d9560b0d969e55cfbe78fcd91164d91aff407a416e98b0" :answer-field/choices ["q-168915/selection/308ff9a17aa98dbca82d5392a2b9f27bc530d98cf03a2265d0d33aae3a283544" "q-168915/selection/f56249ca5a5eb9a722d9560b0d969e55cfbe78fcd91164d91aff407a416e98b0" "q-168915/selection/f083c172cff50ef1b5db3ddb2b53cb5cf94037d4eb64381d570a95d999942d12" "q-168915/selection/9117ee8e5cf9bfe4d16f1a3c00f2f3ceaf688cfd6a5494efb43d7b70fb965afa" "q-168915/selection/2566b7de21c1a242869bd1f8943f91906094c82ae33ab3c11392b9c6a4fee6db"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-168915" :question/id #uuid "e48ff996-e051-5d4b-b71b-b5bb6808f76c" :question/math-academy-id "q-168915" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(1)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We have a decoupled system. Therefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(1)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(1) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3(1)}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{1} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}{e}^{3} \\\\ {c}_{2}e\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3} \\\\ -{e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{-3}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}-{e}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -{e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-168915/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cec0e48f-9fbb-5ada-b7fd-0d389d1b7438"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-168915"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186167254 :question/answer-fields 17592186165073] {:db/id "q-39268/selection/ma-v1/ee32fb066376edcf5d56d0a96d6ff8345ac8dafbe9c255770c689385237a3a00/c99707ad7a03b0dbe05fd170af6f0d3270263c330ec9b4ffe69164a61d0f0cd4" :answer/id #uuid "b3f36854-bad1-5cbb-8fda-af1558fd779d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]{2}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39268/selection/ma-v1/ee32fb066376edcf5d56d0a96d6ff8345ac8dafbe9c255770c689385237a3a00/c2624170c1f10f002b93cd42b3e7acfee22b29fea3f954385ae56709059a7b23" :answer/id #uuid "b1a2a171-c124-5faf-af43-2b786ec7d8f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\end{aligned}]{2}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39268/selection/ma-v1/ee32fb066376edcf5d56d0a96d6ff8345ac8dafbe9c255770c689385237a3a00/24f43e845a4664c4c25b6ccec4fd154ea7ba12c4b2e1d62954a978e2a6e9e951" :answer/id #uuid "30cb1421-5d08-5c47-b480-3fa8b22982fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]{2}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39268/selection/ma-v1/ee32fb066376edcf5d56d0a96d6ff8345ac8dafbe9c255770c689385237a3a00/b810aad12199e02c79c8261059a13519d9cafaa38572c07106bebce0590edc28" :answer/id #uuid "6609ee33-982e-5188-9aee-abf75cfb9c74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]{2}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39268/selection/ma-v1/ee32fb066376edcf5d56d0a96d6ff8345ac8dafbe9c255770c689385237a3a00/968838f453c00ff00793e8393f03e77ec00aace4906d44738ba7ba98c88a41cd" :answer/id #uuid "d41f5296-e4cc-54d4-bb1d-338ba647fab7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]{2}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39268/selection/ma-v1/ee32fb066376edcf5d56d0a96d6ff8345ac8dafbe9c255770c689385237a3a00" :answer-field/id #uuid "45b4ad32-c4dc-57a1-a337-899b51bbacd4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-39268/selection/ma-v1/ee32fb066376edcf5d56d0a96d6ff8345ac8dafbe9c255770c689385237a3a00/b810aad12199e02c79c8261059a13519d9cafaa38572c07106bebce0590edc28" :answer-field/choices ["q-39268/selection/ma-v1/ee32fb066376edcf5d56d0a96d6ff8345ac8dafbe9c255770c689385237a3a00/c99707ad7a03b0dbe05fd170af6f0d3270263c330ec9b4ffe69164a61d0f0cd4" "q-39268/selection/ma-v1/ee32fb066376edcf5d56d0a96d6ff8345ac8dafbe9c255770c689385237a3a00/c2624170c1f10f002b93cd42b3e7acfee22b29fea3f954385ae56709059a7b23" "q-39268/selection/ma-v1/ee32fb066376edcf5d56d0a96d6ff8345ac8dafbe9c255770c689385237a3a00/24f43e845a4664c4c25b6ccec4fd154ea7ba12c4b2e1d62954a978e2a6e9e951" "q-39268/selection/ma-v1/ee32fb066376edcf5d56d0a96d6ff8345ac8dafbe9c255770c689385237a3a00/b810aad12199e02c79c8261059a13519d9cafaa38572c07106bebce0590edc28" "q-39268/selection/ma-v1/ee32fb066376edcf5d56d0a96d6ff8345ac8dafbe9c255770c689385237a3a00/968838f453c00ff00793e8393f03e77ec00aace4906d44738ba7ba98c88a41cd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-39268"] :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We have a decoupled system. Therefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{2}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{2}^{0} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =5[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{2}^{t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]{2}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-39268/selection/ma-v1/ee32fb066376edcf5d56d0a96d6ff8345ac8dafbe9c255770c689385237a3a00"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-79726/selection/3e64a546e1e639084b83b77e7e82523b4e3baa359de67adeb8e9bbb4c91dc511" :answer/id #uuid "53e9a019-02c4-5633-acbb-970a0975aba4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{4}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79726/selection/ff2724dd76a9681f801326fb3d169a5266b766cc23791010c856b70640d5c1ae" :answer/id #uuid "669cd908-8e95-51c8-9da3-1ff67c0522e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{2}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79726/selection/f6d5ec8550d12cf8853b27c4640d10549347df23b2fbb2a56a6abef2efd65bdf" :answer/id #uuid "ae848e9e-1a1a-5fb1-91b1-ac4a02311962" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-4} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{2}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79726/selection/eb9137078f498dc2a30199f24e792f1e5bef292b8e7a68d8ef69a4ae8fe696b6" :answer/id #uuid "b8ed83cb-d6a0-5bcb-98d9-fb5a84663ff7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79726/selection/9beb56fe932091bfdf170dd71512dcbe72af815d4177395f5698655f0d1fd7a3" :answer/id #uuid "28b12668-db6e-525c-854d-803423cbac9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{2}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79726/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7dcdf61e-07bc-55cf-b199-a8d3207af65d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79726/selection/9beb56fe932091bfdf170dd71512dcbe72af815d4177395f5698655f0d1fd7a3" :answer-field/choices ["q-79726/selection/3e64a546e1e639084b83b77e7e82523b4e3baa359de67adeb8e9bbb4c91dc511" "q-79726/selection/ff2724dd76a9681f801326fb3d169a5266b766cc23791010c856b70640d5c1ae" "q-79726/selection/f6d5ec8550d12cf8853b27c4640d10549347df23b2fbb2a56a6abef2efd65bdf" "q-79726/selection/eb9137078f498dc2a30199f24e792f1e5bef292b8e7a68d8ef69a4ae8fe696b6" "q-79726/selection/9beb56fe932091bfdf170dd71512dcbe72af815d4177395f5698655f0d1fd7a3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79726" :question/id #uuid "ba37457e-b90f-5fc3-b5f4-b2ba1d277f80" :question/math-academy-id "q-79726" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(2)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-10} \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We have a decoupled system. Therefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{2}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(2)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(2) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-8} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {2}^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-10} \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-8}{c}_{1} \\\\ 4{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{-2}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}+3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{2}^{t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{2}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79726/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cec0e48f-9fbb-5ada-b7fd-0d389d1b7438"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79726"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21120"] :question/problem "Which of the following systems of linear ODEs are decoupled?\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+6{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=7{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=5{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$" :question/worked-solution "A *decoupled system* consists of equations depending on only one variable, such as\n\n$$\nx'_i(t) = \\lambda_i x_i(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda_i$ is a constant. This means that we can solve each equation independently. \n\nWith this in mind, let's examine our systems.\n\n- System I is *not* decoupled because some of its equations depend on more than one variable. For example, $x'_1(t) = 4x_1(t) + 2x_2(t)$ depends on $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t).$\n\n- System II is decoupled since its equations depend on only one variable each. Indeed, $x'_1(t) = -3x_1(t)$ depends on only $x_1(t)$ and $x'_2(t) = 7x_2(t)$ depends on only $x_2(t).$\n\n- System III is *not* decoupled because, for example, the first equation depends on $x_2(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21123"] :question/problem "Find the general solution to the system of differential equations given by\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-6{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a decoupled system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066958/assets/17657d7db880fc0ababc24511039a9d7446952f7521e31ae3351adbb6b28ee61.png)\nthe formula for the general solution is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066958/assets/44a286f1a4c15598038f38cdb4140534bac24caacb36f32ee4ef9cbe05b3e5e1.png)\n\nFirst, we write our differential equation in matrix form:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066958/assets/d9b9ac7fc20d076110f99476fc48d3c00c4206dc37fb2a929893fcbbb77d6526.png)\n\nSince the matrix of the differential system is diagonal, the system is decoupled. \n\nTherefore, the general solution is given by\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066958/assets/4f7cfa979200fccf811a7e0d9a633b7919b33b7740c635a921b75ad09995e700.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21124"] :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066958/assets/5cc29f7492fded69b4100e10329c831cca0734a29966cd1aac2e8ad017636719.png)" :question/worked-solution "We have a decoupled system. Therefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{1t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9)})}^{t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{9}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of $c_1$ and $c_2$ using the initial value $\\mathbf{x}(0).$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{9}^{0} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+(-1)[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{9}^{t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{9}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
